The test calls `_to_rgba_no_colorcycle` with named colors, several hex-string formats, a grayscale string, and tuple RGB/RGBA inputs. Reading the function body shows which branches execute for those inputs: `orig_c = c` is always assigned and later read in the lowercase-name fallback; `c` is reassigned by named-color lookup, lowercase lookup, grayscale conversion, and tuple normalization, then used by later regex checks, tuple-length checks, tuple rebuilding, and the final range check; `match` is assigned by each regex line and immediately tested on the next line; `n` is the comprehension variable in the executed hex-return/list-building lines and is read on the preceding expression line under the benchmark’s line-level convention; `color` is assigned in the 8-digit and 4-digit alpha hex branches and then read in the later return/override lines; `alpha` is assigned only at `alpha = 1` in the 3-tuple branch and then used by the next two lines. The tracked names `elem` and `x` appear only inside generator expressions whose same-line comprehension-local behavior is excluded here, so they contribute no observed pairs.

